---
import EventPosts from './EventPosts.astro';
---
<div class="case-story container">
  <nav class="project-index" aria-label="Projects on this page">
    <a href="#p-research"><span>01</span>Trade-show survey research</a>
    <a href="#p-paris"><span>02</span>Paris community ride</a>
    <a href="#p-film"><span>03</span>Film red-carpet activation</a>
    <a href="#p-shark"><span>04</span>Shark Awareness Day</a>
  </nav>

  <section class="story-section project" id="p-research" aria-labelledby="insta-research">
    <p class="project-tag">01 · market research team</p>
    <h2 id="insta-research">Trade-show survey research</h2>
    <p>I built each survey so the team could compare people who already own an Insta360 with people who don’t yet.</p>
    <ol class="research-steps">
      <li class="research-step">
        <span class="step-num">build</span>
        <h3><strong class="key-number">8</strong> bilingual surveys</h3>
        <p>Programmed in SurveyMonkey and Wenjuanxing for skiing, cycling, mountain biking, and diving shows, then QA’d before each one.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</li>
      <li class="research-step">
        <span class="step-num">clean</span>
        <h3><strong class="key-number">~300</strong> responses</h3>
        <p>Cleaned in Excel with AI-assisted checks, then weighted using the team’s scheme.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</li>
      <li class="research-step key">
        <span class="step-num">compare</span>
        <h3>Buyers vs. prospects</h3>
        <p>Brand awareness, usage, and satisfaction, each measured against competitors.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="work-caption">Results stay with the team. This shows how the study was built.</p>
    <p class="so-what"><span>So what:</span> Splitting buyers from prospects separates two jobs: keeping owners happy and winning new ones.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="story-section project" id="p-paris" aria-labelledby="insta-work">
    <p class="project-tag">02 · brand team</p>
    <h2 id="insta-work">Paris community ride</h2>
    <p>A three-day activation on the Tour de France finale weekend, ending in a <strong class="key-number">90 km</strong> ride with <strong class="key-number">200+ riders</strong>. Working from HQ, I scored sign-ups on riding habits and storytelling to pick <strong class="key-number">100</strong> camera-equipped riders, then wrote one product story two ways: for cyclists and for runners. Each deck covered up to 4 cameras, with <strong class="key-number">12</strong> creator demo videos I picked, 3 per camera.</p>
    <div class="deck-grid">
      <article class="deck-card">
        <div class="deck-visual bike-deck"><h3>The ride.<br />The people.<br />The memories.</h3><svg viewBox="0 0 440 170" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 140C95 150 95 25 195 45S305 150 425 46" stroke-dasharray="6 10" opacity=".45"/><circle cx="147" cy="117" r="30" fill="#FAF8F4"/><circle cx="267" cy="117" r="30" fill="#FAF8F4"/><path d="M147 117L180 64L219 117H147L193 81H249L267 117M238 52H251L249 81M172 62H193M215 18L193 43L210 67L240 70M193 43L174 33"/><circle cx="230" cy="14" r="10" fill="#FAF8F4"/></svg></div>
        <p class="sample-caption">Cycling: hands-free capture, bike mounting, and creator examples.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="deck-card">
        <div class="deck-visual run-deck"><h3>More than<br />the distance.</h3><svg viewBox="0 0 440 170" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17 141C90 74 106 164 174 103S289 160 421 56" stroke-dasharray="6 10" opacity=".45"/><circle cx="232" cy="31" r="12" fill="#FAF8F4"/><path d="M217 53L192 87L221 105L198 143M219 58L247 75L272 53M211 64L177 60L158 79M221 105L252 117L280 106M194 143L181 147M280 106L289 108"/><path d="M306 30V46M298 38H314M123 102V114M117 108H129"/></svg></div>
        <p class="sample-caption">Running: capture the people, places, and moments along the way.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="work-caption">Recreated summaries of my workshop positioning, illustrated for this portfolio.</p>
    <EventPosts />
    <div class="event-links"><a href="https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/think-bold-ride-bold-insta360-takes-over-the-champs-elysees-with-200-rider-community-event-302833050.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official event announcement ↗</a><a href="https://www.rideapart.com/news/803889/insta360s-paris-pop-up-cycling-event-was-crazy-good-please-make-one-for-motorcyclists/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Event photos & recap ↗</a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="story-section project" id="p-film" aria-labelledby="insta-film">
    <p class="project-tag">03 · brand team</p>
    <h2 id="insta-film">Film red-carpet activation</h2>
    <p>I joined planning meetings with the project owner, Insta360’s creative director, and the creator team lead to brainstorm the event plan and creator list for an upcoming studio film. Plans changed after almost every call, so I turned the email threads with the studio and sales teams into one running brief and updated it after each meeting. The studio postponed the premiere, so the activation hasn’t run yet.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="story-section project" id="p-shark" aria-labelledby="insta-shark">
    <p class="project-tag">04 · brand team</p>
    <h2 id="insta-shark">Shark Awareness Day</h2>
    <p>Three partner accounts wanted to share Insta360’s shark footage. I wrote titles and captions and chose images from Insta360’s photo library for their posts, and did the first-round review of the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ca5yzLpq-r4" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official video ↗</a> before final edits.</p>
    <ul class="shark-stats">
      <li><strong>21.2K</strong><span>likes on the @discoversharks post (4M followers)</span></li>
      <li><strong>~4×</strong><span>that account’s median likes on its recent posts</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="work-caption"><a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DaniDfWEQ_f/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">See the post ↗</a> · Median from the account’s 8 most recent posts, checked Oct 2026.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="story-section closing" aria-labelledby="insta-outcome">
    <h2 id="insta-outcome">Reflection</h2>
    <details class="case-reflection">
      <summary>Reflection & what I’d do next <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
      <div class="reflection-copy">
        <h3>Make the selection rubric reusable.</h3>
        <p>I evaluated riding habits and story quality, but the judgment wasn’t formalized. A simple written score for each signal would let teammates screen consistently and make the final selection easier to review.</p>
        <h3>Adapt every example to the audience.</h3>
        <p>The running story was rewritten for runners, but one feature grid still showed bike mounting. Next time I’d adapt the accessories and demonstrations as carefully as the message, using running-specific examples throughout.</p>
        <h3>Agree on measurement before the event.</h3>
        <p>I worked from HQ and didn’t receive data on which selected riders posted. I’d track registration source, selection scores, and post-event content so the team could compare its assumptions with what happened and improve the next shortlist.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>
</div>
<style>
  .project-index { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr)); border:var(--border); background:var(--surface); margin:40px 7px 0 0; }
  .project-index a { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:4px; padding:16px 18px; min-height:44px; color:var(--ink); text-decoration:none; font:400 14px/1.45 var(--font-mono); }
  .project-index a + a { border-left:var(--rule); }
  .project-index a:hover { background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--block) 28%,white); }
  .project-index span { font:700 22px/1 var(--font-display); }
  .case-story .project { scroll-margin-top:24px; border-left:0 !important; padding-left:0 !important; }
  .case-story .project > p + p, .case-story .project > p + ul, .case-story .project > p + ol, .case-story .project > p + div { margin-top:24px; }
  .project-tag { font:500 12px/1.4 var(--font-mono) !important; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.06em; color:var(--muted); margin:0 0 10px !important; }
  .case-story .project > ol, .case-story .project > .deck-grid, .case-story .project > ul { margin-top:24px; }
  .shark-stats { list-style:none; padding:0; margin:24px 10px 0 0; display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); max-width:640px; background:var(--surface); border:var(--border); box-shadow:10px 10px 0 var(--block); }
  .shark-stats li { padding:22px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:8px; }
  .shark-stats li + li { border-left:var(--rule); }
  .shark-stats strong { font:700 40px/1 var(--font-display); letter-spacing:-.02em; }
  .shark-stats span { font:400 14px/1.6 var(--font-mono); }
  @media(max-width:819px) { .project-index { grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); } .project-index a:nth-child(3) { border-left:0; } .project-index a:nth-child(n+3) { border-top:var(--rule); } }
  @media(max-width:420px) { .shark-stats li { padding:18px 16px; } .shark-stats strong { font-size:32px; } }
  .research-sub { color:var(--muted); margin:-8px 0 24px !important; }
  .research-steps { list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0 7px 0 0; display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto minmax(0,1fr) auto minmax(0,1fr); gap:16px; }
  .research-step { background:var(--surface); border:var(--border); box-shadow:7px 7px 0 var(--ink); padding:22px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px; min-width:0; }
  .research-step.key { background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--block) 32%,white); }
  .step-num { font:500 12px/1.4 var(--font-mono); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.06em; color:var(--muted); }
  .research-step h3 { font:600 24px/1.2 var(--font-display); margin:0; }
  .research-step p { font-size:14px !important; line-height:1.65 !important; padding-top:10px; border-top:1px solid var(--rule-soft); }
  .step-arrow { align-self:center; font:400 18px var(--font-mono); color:var(--muted); }
  .so-what { margin-top:28px !important; padding-left:16px; border-left:3px solid var(--accent); font-weight:600 !important; }
  .so-what span { color:var(--accent); }
  .deck-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:24px; }
  .deck-card { min-width:0; }
  .deck-visual { height:330px; border:var(--rule); padding:24px; position:relative; display:flex; flex-direction:column; overflow:hidden; }
  .bike-deck { background:#F7DE69; } .run-deck { background:#DCE9DB; }
  .deck-visual h3 { font:600 42px/1.08 var(--font-display); letter-spacing:-.02em; margin:0; }
  .deck-visual svg { position:absolute; width:86%; right:12px; bottom:20px; height:135px; }
  .bike-deck svg { width:66%; height:110px; bottom:20px; }
  .event-links { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:0 24px; margin-top:20px; }
  .event-links a { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; min-height:44px; font-size:15px; }
  @media(max-width:819px) { .research-steps { grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr); } .step-arrow { justify-self:center; transform:rotate(90deg); } }
  @media(max-width:699px) { .deck-grid { grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr); gap:32px; } .deck-visual { height:310px; } .deck-visual h3 { font-size:36px; } }
</style>
